In article <TOMW.91Jul3041905@orac.esd.sgi.com> tomw@orac.esd.sgi.com (Tom Weinstein) writes:

   In article <1991Jul3.023550.26010@mlb.semi.harris.com>, geg@beep.mis.semi.harris.com (Gregory E. Garland) writes:

   > I've just moved my Sun 3/60 to 4.1.1, so presumably I can use the color
   > xterm submitted to the net by Tom Weinstein. I defined TERMINFO in the
   > config.h file, and made some of the changes he suggested in the termcap.c
   > file; but the compilations barfs on the tparm() function in termcap.c
   > (i.e., can't find it during loading).  So does any kind soul know what
   > the solution to this is? 

   tparm() is part of terminfo.  If you don't have terminfo (which is a
   SysV thing, and I'm not sure if it's in 4.1.1), then you have to make it
   use sprintf to fill out the hilites strings.

SunOS 4.1 and 4.1.1 (I think also 4.0 and 4.0.3) have terminfo support as
well as system V compatible libraries.  There shouldn't be a problem with
compiling nethack to use terminfo in place of termcap.

